config/herdr/sounds/ — linked to ~/.config/herdr/sounds by ./install and ./install --herdr.

request.mp3
    herdr's own "needs attention" sound, copied unmodified from
    https://github.com/herdrdev/herdr, assets/sounds/request.mp3 (identical at v0.9.5,
    git blob fe4859efcc0f215243f960677b9de894d07ab9d7). herdr is licensed under the
    Apache License, Version 2.0: https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0
    Played by claude/hooks/herdr-waiting-bell.sh, so a prose question and a blocked
    dialog sound the same.

silence.mp3
    0.1 s of silence, generated for this repo:
        ffmpeg -f lavfi -i anullsrc=r=44100:cl=mono -t 0.1 -c:a libmp3lame -b:a 32k \
               -map_metadata -1 -fflags +bitexact -flags:a +bitexact silence.mp3
    It is [ui.sound] done_path in config/herdr/config.toml, which is how herdr's
    per-turn "done" sound is muted. docs/HERDR_GUIDE.md section 7.
